      {
        "value": "critically endangered",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "The only people who have any knowledge of OBSL are people over the age of sixty.  These older signers are bilingual in OBSL and Modern Thai Sign Language, but now they rarely use OBSL. It is quite likely that if documentation of OBSL is not completed in one generation that OBSL will be lost to linguistic study forever, since there is currently no extensive record of OBSL. [Endangerment.Certainty: 1]",
        "scale": "elcat-v2024.1"
      },
      {
        "value": "nearly extinct",
        "source": "glottolog-cldf-v5.3",
        "note": "Original Bangkok Sign Language (7187) = Critically Endangered (100 percent certain, based on the evidence available) (OBSL is currently only used in very limited social situations. Instead  MTSL replaces OBSL in almost all interaction. Because of this situation, OBSL is a highly endangered sign language. It is quite likely that if documentation of OBSL is not completed in one generation that OBSL will be lost to linguistic study forever, since there is currently no extensive record of OBSL.) [Woodward et al. 2015](cldf:woodward:james:etal:15:3)",
